Package: MRBMA
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Model Averaging for Multivariable Mendelian Randomization
Version: 0.1.0
Date: 2026-05-23
Authors@R: c(
    person("Leonardo", "Bottolo", email = "lb664@cam.ac.uk",       role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Verena",   "Zuber",   email = "v.zuber@imperial.ac.uk", role = "aut"))
Maintainer: Leonardo Bottolo <lb664@cam.ac.uk>
Description: Implements the MR-BMA method of Zuber et al. (2020)
    <doi:10.1038/s41467-019-13870-3> for prioritising causal exposures from
    genome-wide summary statistics using Bayesian model averaging (BMA). Two
    complementary search strategies are provided: exhaustive enumeration of all
    2^d - 1 possible models via MRBMA_exhaustive(), which is feasible for up to
    approximately 12 exposures, and a shotgun stochastic search (SSS) via
    MRBMA_SSS() for larger model spaces, based on the algorithm of Hans et al.
    (2007) <doi:10.1198/016214507000000121>. Both strategies return
    model-averaged causal estimates and Marginal Posterior Probabilities of
    Inclusion (MPPIs) for each exposure. Empirical p-values and
    Benjamini-Hochberg false discovery rates are obtained through the permutation
    procedure of Levin et al. (2021) <doi:10.1161/CIRCULATIONAHA.121.053797>.
    Diagnostic functions detect influential and outlying genetic instruments using
    Cook's distance (Cook (1977) <doi:10.1080/00401706.1977.10489493>) and a
    Q-statistic. All inner-loop matrix computations are implemented in C++ via
    RcppArmadillo; the stochastic search hash table uses std::unordered_map.
